msgid "Migrate from Panache to Quarkus Data Hibernate"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide helps you migrate an existing Hibernate ORM with Panache or Hibernate Reactive with Panache application to Quarkus Data Hibernate.\n"
"Both migration paths use managed, stateful sessions to preserve persistence-context and dirty-checking behavior.\n"
"Follow <<orm-migration,Hibernate ORM with Panache>> for Hibernate ORM or <<reactive-migration,Hibernate Reactive with Panache>> for Hibernate Reactive."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For complete API descriptions, see xref:hibernate-orm-panache.adoc[Hibernate ORM with Panache],\n"
"xref:hibernate-reactive-panache.adoc[Hibernate Reactive with Panache], and the\n"
"xref:quarkus-data-hibernate.adoc[Quarkus Data Hibernate reference guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus Data Hibernate is currently experimental. Its APIs may change."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate ORM with Panache"
msgstr "Hibernate ORM with Panache"

msgid "Prepare the application"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus Data Hibernate generates repository implementations and metamodel accessors at build time.\n"
"Enable its annotation processor and add the required extension by following the\n"
"xref:quarkus-data-hibernate-getting-started.adoc[Quarkus Data Hibernate getting started tutorial]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Remove the `quarkus-hibernate-orm-panache` extension when converting the application.\n"
"Classic Panache extensions and Quarkus Data Hibernate cannot be used together in the same application."
msgstr ""

msgid "Your existing entity mappings, datasource configuration, Hibernate ORM configuration, and transaction boundaries remain applicable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Understand the repository changes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With Panache, you define custom query methods either as static methods on the entity class, following the active-record\n"
"pattern, or as instance methods in a separate repository class."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your application uses active record, move custom static query methods to a repository interface as default methods or generated query methods.\n"
"Nesting the repository inside the entity lets you access it through the entity's generated Jakarta Persistence metamodel:\n"
"`Person.list(...)` becomes `Person_.repo().list(...)`."
msgstr ""

msgid "For applications using Panache repository classes, replace each class with a repository interface and convert custom method implementations to default methods or generated query methods."
msgstr ""

msgid "Both nested and top-level repository interfaces support injection."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The examples below use `ManagedEntity` and `ManagedRepository` to preserve Panache's stateful persistence-context and dirty-checking behavior.\n"
"For details about session models, see xref:quarkus-data-hibernate.adoc#session-and-access-models[Session and access models]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Migrate an active-record entity"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`PanacheEntity` combines an inherited generated `Long` identifier, instance persistence operations, and common\n"
"operations such as `Person.list(...)`, `Person.listAll()`, and `Person.count()` , called directly on the entity class.\n"
"`ManagedEntity` retains the identifier and instance operations, but does not provide static query methods.\n"
"Instead, these operations are provided by ManagedRepository and can be accessed through Person_.repo() on the generated\n"
"metamodel."
msgstr ""

