msgstr ""

msgid "to a call on the nested repository in the generated Jakarta Persistence metamodel:"
msgstr ""

msgid "or to call on an injected repository:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Move custom static methods"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Move custom static query helpers from the entity into a repository default method, a generated `@Find`, `@Query`, or `@Delete` method, or an application service.\n"
"For example, migrate this Panache entity method:"
msgstr ""

msgid "to a default method on the nested repository:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Then migrate the call site:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alternatively, call `Person_.repo().findAlive()` through the generated metamodel.\n"
"For examples of generated query methods, see <<generated-repository-methods>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Migrate a Panache repository"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Replace a handwritten CDI repository implementation with an interface.\n"
"Quarkus Data generates its CDI implementation at build time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The entity uses `ManagedEntity`, as in the previous section.\n"
"When using this top-level repository, there's no need for a nested `Repo` interface in the entity itself.\n"
"Replace the `@ApplicationScoped` class with the `@Repository` interface and use `default` for custom method\n"
"implementations.\n"
"You can also declare annotated methods whose implementations are generated, and take this a step further:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The top-level interface above uses `jakarta.data.repository.Repository`; a nested `Person.Repo` does not need this annotation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Injection and query call sites remain the same before and after this conversion:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Migrate entity identifiers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`PanacheEntity` maps directly to `ManagedEntity`: both provide a generated `Long` identifier.\n"
"For a `PanacheEntityBase` entity with an application-defined identifier, retain its `@Id` mapping, implement `ManagedEntity.CustomId`, and use `ManagedRepository.CustomId<Entity, Id>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you use a top-level Panache repository with a custom identifier, migrate it to a top-level interface instead of declaring the nested `Repo` above:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you want an inherited generated identifier of another type, Quarkus Data also provides `WithId.AutoString`, `WithId.AutoUUID`, and `WithId.AutoUUIDv7`.\n"
"See xref:quarkus-data-hibernate.adoc#about-entity-identifiers[entity identifiers] for details."
msgstr ""

msgid "Migrate common operations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Most Panache repository and entity operations are available from `ManagedRepository` and `ManagedEntity` with the same names.\n"
"The following table shows the usual replacements."
msgstr ""

msgid "Panache"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus Data Hibernate"
msgstr ""

msgid "`persist(entity)`, `persistAndFlush(entity)`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`repository.persist(entity)`, `repository.persistAndFlush(entity)`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`delete(entity)`, `isPersistent(entity)`, `flush()`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The corresponding `ManagedRepository` methods."
msgstr ""

msgid "`entity.persist()`, `entity.persistAndFlush()`, `entity.delete()`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The same instance operations after the entity extends `ManagedEntity` or implements `ManagedEntity.CustomId`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`findById(id)`, `findByIdOptional(id)`, `deleteById(id)`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The same `ManagedRepository` operations."
msgstr ""

msgid "`count()`, `count(query, parameters)`, `delete(query, parameters)`, `deleteAll()`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The corresponding `ManagedRepository` methods return `Long` instead of `long`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`update(query, parameters)`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`repository.update(query, parameters)`, returning `Long` instead of `int`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`find()`, `list()`, `stream()` and their `*All` variants"
msgstr ""

msgid "The same operations, except that sorting is applied to the query object. See <<sorting>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "`getEntityManager()` or `getSession()`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`repository.getSession()` for entity-bound work. Inject `Session` or `EntityManager` for general-purpose access."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The blocking `persist()`, `persistAndFlush()`, `delete(entity)`, `entity.delete()`, and `flush()` operations return `Void` instead of `void`.\n"
"The `isPersistent()` and `deleteById()` operations return `Boolean` instead of `boolean`.\n"
"Existing calls that ignore a `Void` result or unbox a `Boolean` or `Long` result can retain their usual form.\n"
"For bulk updates, change variables and custom method return types that receive the count from `int` to `long` or `Long`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "If an existing API must still return `int`, convert explicitly with `Math.toIntExact(people.update(...))`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`ManagedRepository` supports the indexed `Object...` and named `Map<String, Object>` parameter forms used by Panache.\n"
"Replace deprecated Panache `Parameters` instances with a `Map`, for example `Map.of(\"status\", Status.ALIVE)`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`findByIds(List<?>)` has no inherited `ManagedRepository` counterpart.\n"
"Declare a repository method such as `@Query(\"where id in :ids\") List<Person> findByIds(List<UUID> ids)`, or use a dynamic query such as `repository.list(\"id in ?1\", ids)` with the actual identifier attribute name and type."
msgstr ""

